{"question_id": "a89d7624", "hypothesis": "Based on your past conversations, I know you're a music enthusiast who loves Denver's music scene, enjoyed The Killers at Red Rocks, and even met Brandon Flowers after the show! Here's a tailored itinerary for your Denver trip:\n\n## \ud83c\udfb5 Music Venues to Check Out\nSince you loved Red Rocks, here are other Denver venues you shouldn't miss:\n\n1. **Red Rocks Amphitheater** \u2014 You already know the magic, but check if any shows are happening during your visit!\n2. **The Ogden Theatre** \u2014 Historic venue in LoDo with indie, rock, and electronic acts in an intimate setting\n3. **The Bluebird Theater** \u2014 Another historic spot featuring singer-songwriters and rock\n4. **The Fillmore Auditorium** \u2014 Iconic venue hosting rock and hip-hop acts\n5. **Larimer Lounge** \u2014 Smaller, laid-back venue perfect for discovering new talent\n6. **The hi-dive** \u2014 Bar and venue focused on punk, indie, and alternative\n7. **The Marquis Theater** \u2014 Mid-sized venue with rock, pop, hip-hop, and electronic\n\n## \ud83c\udfb6 Festivals to Look Into\nDepending on when you visit, check out:\n- **Grandoozy** \u2014 Rock, pop, hip-hop, and electronic\n- **Denver Folk Festival** \u2014 Folk, bluegrass, and roots\n- **Denver Jazz Festival** \u2014 Jazz in all its forms\n- **Westword Music Showcase** \u2014 One-day festival highlighting local and national acts\n- **Riot Fest Denver** \u2014 Punk, rock, and alternative (happens in September)\n\n## \ud83c\udfa7 Music Shopping\n- **Twist & Shout Records** \u2014 A legendary record store", "verdict": "yes", "question_type": "single-session-preference"}
