{"question_id": "6222b6eb", "hypothesis": "Based on our previous conversation on May 21, 2023, the answer is clear:\n\n**6S** (Second Simulation of a Satellite Signal in the Solar Spectrum) is the algorithm implemented in the **SIAC_GEE** tool.\n\nSpecifically, as I mentioned in that conversation:\n\n> \"6S (Second Simulation of a Satellite Signal in the Solar Spectrum) algorithm, is a radiative transfer model that simulates the interactions between electromagnetic radiation and the Earth's atmosphere, land, and water surfaces. **It is implemented in the SIAC_GEE (Sentinel-2 Image Atmospheric Correction in Google Earth Engine) tool.**\"\n\nThis was also confirmed earlier in the same conversation when comparing SIAC_GEE and Sen2Cor:\n\n> \"SIAC_GEE uses the **6S radiative transfer model** for atmospheric correction, while Sen2Cor uses the L2A_Process algorithm.\"\n\nSo to summarize the three methods and their implementations:\n1. **6S** \u2192 implemented in **SIAC_GEE** (runs on Google Earth Engine)\n2. **MAJA** \u2192 implemented in MAJA software (developed by CNES, the French Space Agency)\n3. **Sen2Cor** \u2192 implemented in Sen2Cor software (developed by ESA)", "verdict": "yes", "question_type": "single-session-assistant"}
